# EPIC-04.7 — Board Members & Email Invitations

## Goal

Implement board member management and invitation system.

Users must be able to:

- view board members
- invite members by email
- accept invitations
- assign tasks to board members
- manage member roles
- remove members from a board

Invitations are sent using **email addresses**, but once accepted,
users must be linked to the board using **userId**.

---

# Functional Overview

Each board has a list of members.

A board member contains:

- boardId
- userId
- role (ADMIN | MEMBER)

Users can invite new members by email.

If the invited email belongs to an existing user,
they can immediately join the board.

If the email does not exist yet,
an invitation is stored and the user joins after registration.

---

# GraphQL Operations Used

## Queries

boardMembers(boardId)

Returns all members of the board.

pendingInvites(boardId)

Returns all pending invitations.

pendingInvitesByEmail(email)

Returns invites sent to a specific email.

---

## Mutations

inviteBoardMember

inviteByEmail

updateBoardMemberRole

removeBoardMember

---

# Tasks Implementation

---

# 1. Fetch Board Members

Load all board members.

Query:

boardMembers(boardId)

Each member must display:

- user name
- email
- role
- avatar (optional)

Members appear in:

- board settings
- task assignee selector

---

# 2. Fetch Pending Invitations

Load invitations for the board.

Query:

pendingInvites(boardId)

Each invite must show:

- invited email
- role
- inviter
- created date

---

# 3. Invite Member by Email

Users must be able to invite a member via email.

UI:

Invite Member Modal

Fields:

email (required)

role (ADMIN | MEMBER)

Mutation used:

inviteByEmail

---

# 4. Accept Invitation

When a user registers with an email that has pending invites:

Query:

pendingInvitesByEmail(email)

The user can accept the invitation.

When accepted:

- userId is linked to the board
- invite is removed

---

# 5. Update Member Role

Admins must be able to change roles.

Editable roles:

ADMIN

MEMBER

Mutation:

updateBoardMemberRole

---

# 6. Remove Member

Admins can remove members.

Mutation:

removeBoardMember

After removal:

- user loses access to board
- tasks assigned to them remain but show unknown user

---

# 7. Task Assignee Integration

Tasks must reference users via:

assigneeId

The assignee selector must list **board members only**.

